prompt_template:
Create an editorial poster in the "Monochrome Tech-Grid Editorial" visual style.

Subject: {SUBJECT}
Action: {SUBJECT_ACTION}
Prop/Product: {PRODUCT_OR_PROP}
Location: {LOCATION}
Background: {BACKGROUND_ELEMENTS}
Main text: {MAIN_TEXT}
Secondary text: {SECONDARY_TEXT}
Accent symbol: {ACCENT_SYMBOL}
Wardrobe/styling: {WARDROBE_STYLE}
Style fidelity anchors: {STYLE_FIDELITY_ANCHORS}
Source content to avoid: {SOURCE_CONTENT_TO_AVOID}

Match the style fidelity anchors before introducing content novelty. Build a severe Swiss-influenced three-scale hierarchy: an immense ultra-bold black neo-grotesk headline tight to the outer edges; a dense field of small technical modules separated by hairline rules; and one large black-and-white documentary photograph cropped decisively at the frame edges. For 9:16, stack headline, technical information field, then photograph so the photograph occupies roughly the lower half. For 16:9, let the headline span the top and combine a left information rail with a photograph dominating the right and lower field.

Use warm off-white uncoated paper, charcoal-black ink, subtle dry-offset grain, fine scratches, rubbed edges, and only slight analog misregistration. Keep the photograph strictly monochrome with crisp documentary daylight, deep blacks, controlled pale highlights, and a straightforward 35–50 mm viewpoint. Use one tiny safety-red warning or directional block and, optionally, one miniature yellow-and-blue calibration strip; accents together must remain below three percent of the image.

Typography must be intentional and readable: set the exact short headline "{MAIN_TEXT}" in oversized tightly tracked grotesk type; use "{SECONDARY_TEXT}" only as concise small supporting copy. Add a few plausible fictional serial numbers, coordinates, revision marks, outlined cells, data bars, registration crosses, line diagrams, the simple symbol {ACCENT_SYMBOL}, and hatched blocks. Do not add scannable QR codes, real barcodes, real logos, brands, watermarks, signatures, usernames, or creator marks.

Avoid glossy 3D, gradients, colorful advertising, cinematic color grading, soft lifestyle minimalism, scrapbook collage, fisheye perspective, random UI widgets, excessive visual noise, fake paragraphs, illegible glyphs, and any literal source content. Important content rule: preserve the visual system and density while changing the subject, action, prop, setting, text, identity, and story premise completely.
